{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 38c7c579: option (a). P1 gets its own role table beside\nits own definition. The shipped Lending package does not change.\n\nReason: a role table belongs to the package whose acts use its\nactions. Only the second definition has an act that needs\n`lending.publish`. The shipped definition has none, so a grant in the\nshipped table gives a room an action that no act of its definition\naccepts. The release also stays whole: CUT-R signs the shipped package\nat R1 main, and P1 is a side lane that the stable base does not wait\nfor.\n\nRules for P1:\n\n1. P1 changes none of these files: `examples/lending/roles.ts`,\n   `dap.application.json`, `package.ts`, `definition.ts`,\n   `definition.json`, `pin.ts` and, after R1, the Lending identifier\n   file. P1 changes no release constant and no hosted configuration.\n2. The P1 source lives in `examples/lending/publisher/`: the second\n   definition, its role table, the publication map, the publisher\n   module, the two scripts and the witnesses.\n3. The P1 role table takes each row of `lendingRoles.roles` and adds\n   `lending.publish` to `agent`. It copies no row by hand.\n4. The second definition is a package with another name:\n   `ai.generalbusiness.lending.publisher`, version `0.1.0`. Write a\n   manifest for it only when a witness or a script reads the manifest.\n   Your source plan states which one reads it. P1 makes no release, no\n   signature and no trust row for that package.\n\nThis ruling replaces item 4 of request bea87570. The other items and\nthe conditions stay.\n\nThe note names the shipped files in section 4.2. I carry that\ncorrection to Hugh with the other note changes. The P1 implementation\nnote states the difference in one sentence and cites this ruling.\n\nThe publisher definition replaces the shipped one in a later release\nhead, with a new package version and a new signed release. That head\nis not P1, and I file it after the P2 note.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}